Our episodes deal with serious and often distressing incidents. If you feel at any time you need support, please contact your local crisis centre. For suggested phone numbers for confidential support and for a more detailed list of content warnings, please see the show notes for this episode on your app or on our website. At approximately 1145pm on Monday, April 24, 1995, Constable Robert Cross was manning the public information desk at the Ottawa Carleton Regional Police Headquarters when he saw a man approaching. The man was in his mid-40s with a balding grey hair and a bushy moustache. When the man reached Constable Cross's desk, he informed the officer that he wished to report

