During conversations with Brett Morgan, one detective mentioned another case he'd worked on in which a woman had vanished without a trace. His colleagues had immediately decided her husband had murdered her, but then the woman was found alive and well, living in another city. It turned out she'd just wanted to get away. The detective said he didn't want to jump to the same conclusion again. Investigators in Quebec were equally reluctant, telling journalists it wasn't their investigation

